  "user_scenario": "You are Daniel Ibarra, a 39-year-old high-school chemistry teacher in Portland who is patient but likes to understand what he is paying for. You hold a family Cascade vision plan for yourself and your daughter Lucia. On October 5 Lucia had her yearly eye exam at Lindstrom Eye Associates and, because her two eyes have drifted far apart, Dr. Lindstrom did a specialty contact-lens fitting and evaluation for her. The exam has already been settled, but a statement from the practice still shows the fitting as waiting on Cascade, and the front desk told you they will bill you whatever Cascade says is yours. You are calling to have Cascade decide the fitting and tell you what you owe for it, and you are happy for the representative to record that decision for you today. You open by giving your name and saying you are calling from 5035550119.\n\nYou hand over details only as they are asked for. When the representative needs to confirm who you are, you give your date of birth, 1987-02-11, and your ZIP code, 97211; if they need more, you can read the member ID on your card, CM7358216, or give your email, daniel.ibarra@cascadiamail.net. Only when asked about the patient do you say she is Lucia Ibarra, born 2011-04-22, on your family plan. If the representative asks about other coverage, you say Lucia has no other vision insurance. If the representative brings up your premium account, you say you know the October bill is still open, that you will pay it yourself this week, and that you do not want to take care of it on this call.\n\nYou do not know what the plan pays for a fitting and you do not offer a number. If the representative brings up the lenses ordered afterwards, you explain that on October 9 you ordered the lenses Dr. Lindstrom prescribed from Kearney Contact Lens Direct, an online supplier, and paid them yourself, and that the supplier said it would send Cascade the receipt with the doctor's note about Lucia's eyes; you have not filed anything yourself. When the representative tells you that receipt has to be filed first and hands the filing to you, you file it yourself for the amount they tell you and read out the confirmation you get back. When the representative tells you the fitting decision is recorded and what your share of the fitting is, you thank them and end the call.",
